IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `P1-art-6b`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-tests-art-6b.l4 -- tests of Art 6(3) and (4).  Expected values written from the text (src:97-106).
-- ============================================================================

§ `Art 6(3): the legal basis`

-- legal obligation laid down by Union law
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- official authority laid down by Member State law to which the controller is subject
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Member State law to which the controller is not subject
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- laid down by neither
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not covered: the other bases
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `Art 6(1)(a) consent` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `Art 6(1)(b) contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the basis for the processing is laid down by Union law or by Member State law to which the controller is subject` `Art 6(1)(f) legitimate interests` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 6(3): the purpose`

#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- point (c): the alternative "necessary for the performance of a task" is for point (e) only
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` `Art 6(1)(c) legal obligation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` `Art 6(1)(e) public interest or official authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the purpose of the processing is determined in the legal basis or, for point (e), is necessary for the task` `Art 6(1)(b) contract` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 6(3): matters a legal basis may adapt ("inter alia": the list is open)`

#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) the general conditions governing the lawfulness of processing by the controller` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) the types of data which are subject to the processing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) the data subjects concerned` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) the entities to which the personal data may be disclosed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) the purposes for which the personal data may be disclosed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) the purpose limitation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) storage periods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) processing operations and processing procedures, including measures to ensure lawful and fair processing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not covered: a matter the list does not name
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the legal basis may contain specific provisions to adapt the application of the rules of this Regulation on the matter` `Art 6(3) some other matter` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 6(3): the law meets an objective of public interest and is proportionate`

#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the Union or Member State law meets an objective of public interest and is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the Union or Member State law meets an objective of public interest and is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the Union or Member State law meets an objective of public interest and is proportionate to the legitimate aim pursued` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Art 6(4): processing for another purpose`

-- the gate holds (another purpose, no consent, no qualifying law) and all five matters were weighed
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes`, `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected`, `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data`, `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects`, `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- the order does not matter, and further matters ("inter alia") change nothing
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4) some other matter`, `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes`, `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected`, `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data`, `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects`, `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`

-- the gate holds and matter )(a was not weighed
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected`, `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data`, `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects`, `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the gate holds and matter )(b was not weighed
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes`, `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data`, `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects`, `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the gate holds and matter )(c was not weighed
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes`, `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected`, `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects`, `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the gate holds and matter )(d was not weighed
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes`, `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected`, `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data`, `Art 6(4)(e) the existence of appropriate safeguards`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the gate holds and matter )(e was not weighed
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4)(a) any link between the purposes`, `Art 6(4)(b) the context in which the personal data have been collected`, `Art 6(4)(c) the nature of the personal data`, `Art 6(4)(d) the possible consequences of the intended further processing for data subjects`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the gate holds and nothing was weighed
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- "inter alia" alone is not enough
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE FALSE (LIST `Art 6(4) some other matter`) EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- the gate does not hold: the processing is for the original purpose
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- the gate does not hold: another purpose but based on the data subject's consent
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE TRUE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- the gate does not hold: another purpose but based on a qualifying law
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the controller takes into account the matters (a) to (e) in ascertaining whether processing for another purpose is compatible` TRUE FALSE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- the regulative form, traced
#TRACE `Art 6(4) the controller must take into account the matters (a) to (e)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 6(4) take into account the matters (a) to (e) to ascertain whether processing for another purpose is compatible` AT 5
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 6(4) the controller must take into account the matters (a) to (e)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- expected: the obligation is still standing; the text states no time limit, so it is never a breach
#TRACE `Art 6(4) the controller must take into account the matters (a) to (e)` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- expected: FULFILLED, because the gate does not hold
